While the firmware will complain, the ECU is not required to run Linux on
Alpha

The ECU is needed to setup the eisa interrupt data for UNIX and some ARC/NT
This info was kept in firmware so the OS knew how to talk to the eisa
modules that were installed.

For Linux, it's not needed, the kernel does the setup during the init
sequence.

there is a separate ECU for  Unix and NT  your best bet is someone in this
group, as it was third-party software (Not Compaq)  Use the unix version and
just accept all the defaults.

JJ

