Michael Keller <m@ike.ch> writes:
> I assume you mean the Mylex DAC 960 when you speak of RAID.
> 
> You'll find a short manual for the installation in article [1].

Addition to that article is that be very careful in picking the dac960 
firmware, I tried to flash 3.x fw to card that could only support 2.72 version
due to flash memory size. Thank camel it did not work. 

I didn't install suse, I did isntall rh7.1 and I had to first attach a 
scsi disk to scsi card in the machine, install to that disk, then
compile more recent kernel, boot it and copy the running system to
raid. Works well. When creating the partition table with fdisk, don't
start first partition from cyl 1, use instead 5 or some other small number.
This is because you'll want to leave space for aboot for booting off
the raid and not having your partition table overwritten each time
you install aboot. (I had to try that a few times :-) Correct partition
table type for alpha is BSD disklabel, at least for the raid set that
you want to use for booting.

