I'm not much beyond newbie myself, but I think I stumbled onto
something that helped me.  (I have installed RH6.1 a few times,
then RH7.0 and RH7.1.)

When the installer is first getting started, _before_ you get to
disk partitioning and such, you can hit ALT-CTRL-F2 (or one of
the other function keys--check the documentation) and get to a
text console.  From this text console, you can run fdisk manually
to set up your partitions.  If you're booting from SRM, make sure
you use BSD-style partitioning alias disk labels instead of the
alternative.  And, in case this isn't obvious, if you have any
live data on the machine, _BE_ _VERY_ _CAREFUL_!

Good luck.

