If I remember correctly from a few years ago when I was in
processor design at a large company (name starts with 'I'), we
were told the philosophy of the Alpha design team was to not
spend much effort with fancy clock gating and other methods to
reduce average power when the processor was idle.  If this is
correct, it would indicate that the power draw and heat output
would not differ much between the CPU being idle and heavily
loaded.

If you can get your hands on a power supply (or a small number of
them) that meet(s) API's specifications, it might be worth a try,
but don't quote me on that.

