I've seen this problem with both vendor PS's and API approved PS's
so I don't consider it a PS issue. It could be heat on a particular
chip (seen this on AMD systems) or as you've noticed, an issue
with seating parts. I found re-seating the processor and the memory
made the problem go away for substantial periods of time so I'm
inclined to believe it's contact issues with parts inserted into
the board working their way slightly loose. It may not be thermal,
vibrations could do it too. Or, oxidation of some sort on the contacts.

Wes


