> monitor is the same as teh SRM console, however I did do that, and there is
> no change. I'm really lost as to what I should do to get into the SRM
> console or just back into ARC. Hope someone can help.

Despite what you've heard, I don't believe that the PC64 EEPROM has room 
for both SRM and ARC console firmware.  I hosed mine by trying to 
install both and was forced into a painful recovery using the service 
port (DECnet connector on the front of the board), an old DOS PC and 
some obscure utility from the EBDK (evaluation board deverloper kit).  I 
think Hewlett-Digi-Paq (or whatever they're called this week) finally 
made the console firmware available on their ftp site.  If you really 
need the SRM console (I did to support Tru64), then plan on it being the 
only thing resident.

Even with SRM on board, you can always run ARC from a floppy disk (e.g. 
for executing RAID controller config software.)

Steve




