Do you get the 
aboot>
-prompt? Booting from rh7.1 cdrom should first give you a list of 
available kernels and this is done by bootstrap program named "aboot".
I think the "jumping to bootstrap code" happens before that. 
One thing worth checking might be boot flags from SRM .. for aboot
the "boot_flags" might be empty so saying
set boot_flags ""
and then
boot dka600
might do something. 
also "show *" or "show" or "show all" (can't remember just now and I'd like 
to not bring this box down to srm just for checking) shows the srm parameters
and you just might want to check them all, there should be less than 200 of 
them :-)

boot dka600 -file /kernels/vmlinux.gz -flags "root=/dev/scd0 initrd=images/ramdisk.img text"

might try booting the kernel via aboot from dka600 with no need for 
user intervention. Also you might want to read

http://www.redhat.com/docs/manuals/linux/RHL-7.1-Manual/alpha-install-guide/

