"JohnJ" <john.jemiolo@mindspring.com> writes:
> If it's the digital raid, with a V2 rom it is not supported by Linux,  you
> need the 960 with 2 firmware sockets and V3 roms that populate both sockets.

Not true, but you need to upgrade your 960 to firmware version 2.73, found
from here:
http://www.mylex.com/support/productgd/matrix.html#old-dac
(and this fw is propably not supported by Compaq) and be careful in 
identifying your 960, there's several dozen different models, like
mine that is DAC960PU-3. Utility to flash said fw is here:
ftp://gatekeeper.research.compaq.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/v6.1/utility/swxcrmgr/ra200fl.exe
from same place the program ra200rcu.exe can be used to config the card, 
at least my card did hose up its configuration when fw was upgraded from
2.4something to 2.73. 

With this fw 2.73 you'll need linux kernel v2.4.11 or newer or 2.2.11 if
willing to use 2.2 -series. For example rh7.1 installation cd has 
older kernel. Debian alpha might have more recent kernel but it did not 
like my TLZ09 :-)

http://www.dandelion.com/Linux/DAC960.html has more info about said card.

